  "notes": "TIER A (UK): REAL primary-source ONS LCF data, ad-hoc Table 5 'Detailed household expenditure by household composition', UK FYE 2024. All \u00a3/week figures converted to ANNUAL via x52.1786, kept in nominal GBP (local currency; frontend applies PPP conversion). GROUP LABELS (source header structure, spanning two logical super-groups): 'Retired households' split by pension type (State pension / Other retired) x household size (One person / Two adults); 'Non-retired' households split by size only (One person / Two adults, no children distinction in this column set); and a combined 'Retired and non-retired households' block split by adult count x child count (One adult with one child / Two adults with one or more children / One or two adults with one child / One or two adults with two or more children -- the source's last two columns partially overlap conceptually with the first two of this block per the header merge cells, an ambiguity in the original ONS table's column spanning that we have preserved via the literal group names rather than resolving by guesswork). NOTE: unlike US CES's by-household-type file, this table does NOT include a clean 'couple_no_kids' / 'single_parent' taxonomy matching the v2 schema's example group names -- ONS's own household-composition cuts for FYE2024 in this ad-hoc release are retirement-status-first, not family-structure-first; consuming code should treat the 'group' field values as free-text labels rather than assuming exact string matches against the schema's illustrative examples (couple_no_kids, etc.). avg_income_before_tax and avg_income_after_tax are NULL for all groups -- this ad-hoc release's Table 5 reports EXPENDITURE only, no income figures by household composition; ONS's income-by-household-type series (via the Effects of Taxes and Benefits release) uses a different household typology and was not joined here to avoid a low-confidence cross-table merge; flagged as a gap rather than fabricated. housing_owner_share is NULL for all groups -- no tenure-by-household-composition cross-tab was located for FYE2024 within the task budget (only tenure-by-INCOME-DECILE was available, used in the sibling uk_lcf.json file instead). CATEGORY MAPPING: identical methodology to uk_lcf.json (by-decile file) -- see that file's notes for full COICOP-row-to-schema mapping detail. Key difference: in THIS household-composition table, ONS does NOT suppress the Health (row 6) or Education (row 10) rows for disclosure reasons (unlike the by-decile table), so healthcare_oop and education are populated with real values here where by-decile they are null -- education is itself heavily null/suppressed within specific household types too (only nonretired_two_adults, one_or_two_adults_with_one_child, and one_or_two_adults_with_two_or_more_children report non-null education spend, consistent with those being the groups most likely to have school-age children). avg_expenditure_total = ONS's own published 'Total expenditure' row (sum of groups 1-13); voluntary_savings (row 14.6, 'Other items recorded') sits outside this total per ONS convention, same caveat as the by-decile file. All dollar figures nominal 2024 GBP, not inflation-adjusted to another base year."
